{"claims":[{"claim":"Databricks row filters and masks, is_account_group_member, three-level namespace and grants follow the docs verified in Track A.","source":"https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/filters-and-masks/manually-apply and related pages (checked 2026-09-25)","status":"verified"},{"claim":"SELECT * EXCEPT (col) is supported in Databricks SQL.","source":"https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/sql/language-manual/sql-ref-syntax-qry-star (checked 2026-09-25)","status":"verified"}],"concept_html":"<p>Eight snippets of Databricks SQL and DAX, each with one seeded bug. SQL and DAX look simple, which makes their bugs easy to read past. The answer key stays hidden until you submit.</p>\n<p><strong>What to look for in Databricks SQL:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Syntax from another platform.</strong> <code>CREATE ROW ACCESS POLICY</code> and <code>CREATE MASKING POLICY</code> are Snowflake. Databricks uses a SQL UDF with <code>SET ROW FILTER</code> or <code>SET MASK</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Grants to individuals.</strong> Your standard grants to groups, never to one user's email.</li>\n<li><strong>Group checks.</strong> <code>is_member()</code> checks workspace groups. Unity Catalog guidance favours <code>is_account_group_member()</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Names.</strong> Two-part names resolve against the current catalog. Use three-level names: <code>catalog.schema.table</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Ratios.</strong> An <code>AVG</code> of percentages weights every subgroup equally. Recompute ratios from their sums.</li>\n<li><strong>MERGE sources.</strong> One row per key, or the statement fails.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What to look for in DAX:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Division.</strong> <code>/</code> returns infinity or an error on a zero denominator. <code>DIVIDE</code> returns BLANK.</li>\n<li><strong>Filter context.</strong> <code>ALL(fact_table)</code> removes every filter on the table, wave and region slicers included. Name the one dimension whose filter you mean to remove.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Review each snippet with the same routine: goal, then line by line. For SQL, also check each statement against the Databricks SQL reference in your head: does this statement exist here? The checker tests your fix against the pattern the standard requires. Your score counts bugs found and fixes proposed.</p>\n<p>This lesson closes the practice module. The capstone review in Phase 6 uses the same skills on a whole pull request.</p>","example":{"language":"sql","strong":{"lines":["<span class=\"k\">SELECT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>","<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"k\">SUM</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">weighted_reach</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">NULLIF</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">SUM</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">weighted_base</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reach_pct</span>","<span class=\"k\">FROM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">research_gold</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat_metrics</span>","<span class=\"k\">GROUP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">BY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>"],"notes":[{"html":"Total over total, with the zero base guarded.","line":2}]},"takeaway_html":"<p>For SQL, check the dialect, grants, group functions, names and ratios. For DAX, check DIVIDE and the exact filter each ALL removes.</p>","weak":{"lines":["<span class=\"k\">SELECT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AVG</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">weighted_reach_pct</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reach_pct</span>","<span class=\"k\">FROM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">research_gold</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat_metrics</span>","<span class=\"k\">GROUP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">BY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>"],"notes":[{"html":"An average of subgroup percentages. A subgroup of 12 counts as much as one of 1,200.","line":1}]}},"exercises":[{"code":"CREATE FUNCTION research_governance.region_filter(region STRING)\n  RETURN is_account_group_member(concat('analysts_', region));\nCREATE ROW ACCESS POLICY region_policy ON research_silver.nat_respondents (region);\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"k\">CREATE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">FUNCTION</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">research_governance</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">region_filter</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">STRING</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>","<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">RETURN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is_account_group_member</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">concat</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'analysts_'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>","<span class=\"k\">CREATE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">ROW</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">ACCESS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">POLICY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">region_policy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">ON</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><s