ass=\"w\"> </span>all_brands = CALCULATE ( SUM ( fact_reach[weighted_reach] ), ALL ( fact_reach ) )","<span class=\"nb\">RETURN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">DIVIDE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>this_brand, all_brands )"],"difficulty":4,"fix_brief":{"avoid_html":["ALL ( fact_reach ) removes the wave and region filters too."],"checks":[],"include_html":["Remove only the brand filter: ALL ( dim_brand )."],"must_html":[],"shape":[],"shape_note":"","steps_html":["Change only the line you marked, and the lines it affects.","Keep the rest of the code as it is.","Tap Run checks. A failed check tells you what is still wrong."]},"fix_checker":{"comments":"dax","kind":"text","rules":[{"id":"all_brand","message":"Remove only the brand filter: ALL ( dim_brand ).","pattern":"ALL\\s*\\(\\s*dim_brand\\s*\\)","type":"required"},{"id":"no_all_fact","message":"ALL ( fact_reach ) removes the wave and region filters too.","pattern":"ALL\\s*\\(\\s*fact_reach\\s*\\)","type":"forbidden"}]},"hints":["Which filters does ALL(fact_reach) remove?","All of them.","Name the brand dimension."],"hints_html":["Which filters does ALL(fact_reach) remove?","All of them.","Name the brand dimension."],"id":"D7-L3-E7","language":"dax","packages":[],"primer":"","primer_html":"","prompt":"Goal: each brand's share of weighted reach across all brands, respecting the wave and region slicers. Find the bug and fix it.\n","prompt_html":"<p>Goal: each brand's share of weighted reach across all brands, respecting the wave and region slicers. Find the bug and fix it.</p>","sealed":"","type":"spot_bug","xp":40},{"code":"MERGE INTO research.research_silver.nat_respondents AS t\nUSING research.research_bronze.nat_raw_w14 AS s\nON t.respondent_id = s.respondent_id AND t.wave_id = s.wave_id\nWHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET *\nWHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"n\">MERGE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">INTO</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">research</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">research_silver</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat_respondents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>","<span class=\"k\">USING</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">research</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">research_bronze</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat_raw_w14</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>","<span class=\"k\">ON</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respondent_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respondent_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AND</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wave_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wave_id</span>","<span class=\"k\">WHEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MATCHED</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">THEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">UPDATE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">SET</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span>","<span class=\"k\">WHEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">NOT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MATCHED</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">THEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">INSERT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>"],"difficulty":5,"fix_brief":{"avoid_html":[],"checks":[],"include_html":["Rank rows with ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY respondent_id, wave_id ORDER BY ingestion_timestamp DESC).","Keep only rn = 1."],"must_html":[],"shape":[],"shape_note":"","steps_html":["Change only the line you marked, and the lines it affects.","Keep the rest of the code as it is.","Tap Run checks. A failed check tells you what is still wrong."]},"fix_checker":{"comments":"sql","kind":"text","rules":[{"id":"row_number","message":"Rank rows with ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY respondent_id, wave_id ORDER BY ingestion_timestamp DESC).","pattern":"ROW_NUMBER\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s+OVER\\s*\\(\\s*PARTITION\\s+BY\\s+respondent_id\\s*,\\s*wave_id\\s+ORDER\\s+BY\\s+ingestion_timestamp\\s+DESC\\s*\\)","type":"required"},{"id":"keep_first","message":"Keep only rn = 1.","pattern":"rn\\s*=\\s*1","type":"required"}]},"hints":["Can the source hold two rows for one key?","Yes, and MERGE fails then.","Deduplicate in the USING clause with ROW_NUMBER."],"hints_html":["Can the source hold two rows for one key?","Yes, and MERGE fails then.","Deduplicate in the USING clause with ROW_NUMBER."],"id":"D7-L3-E8","language":"sql","packages":[],"primer":"`MERGE INTO target AS t USING source AS s ON <condition>` is the SQL form of the Delta merge from lesson A3-L1. Each target row is matched against the source rows that meet the `ON` condition:\n\n- `WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET *` overwrites the matched target row with the source row's columns.\n- `WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *` inserts source rows with no match.\n\nThe `USING` part can be a table or a subquery in brackets. In Databricks SQL, `SELECT * EXCEPT (col)` returns every column except `col`.\n","primer_html":"<p><code>MERGE INTO target AS t USING source AS s ON &lt;condition&gt;</code> is the SQL form of the Delta merge from lesson A3-L1. Each target row is matched against the source rows that meet the <code>ON</code> condition:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET *</code> overwrites the matched target row with the source row's columns.</li>\n<li><code>WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *</code> inserts source rows with no match.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <code>USING</code> part can be a table or a subquery in brackets. In Databricks SQL, <code>SELECT * EXCEPT (col)</code> returns every column except <code>col</code>.</p>","prompt":"Goal: MERGE a redelivery into silver. The delivery can repeat a respondent within a wave. Keep the row with the latest `ingestion_timestamp`. Find the bug and fix it.\n","prompt_html":"<p>Goal: MERGE a redelivery into silver. The delivery can repeat a respondent within a wave. Keep the row with the latest <code>ingestion_timestamp</code>. Find the bug and fix it.</p>","sealed":"","type":"spot_bug","xp":50}],"id":"D7-L3","module":"D7","practical":null,"recap":[{"back":"Dialect, grants to groups, is_account_group_member, three-level names, ratios from sums, one source row per MERGE key.","front":"SQL review checklist","id":"D7-L3#0"},{"back":"DIVIDE for every ratio. ALL on the one dimension you mean, never the whole fact table.","front":"DAX review checklist","id":"D7-L3#1"},{"back":"ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY keys ORDER BY ingestion_timestamp DESC), keep rn = 1.","front":"Deduplicating a MERGE source in SQL","id":"D7-L3#2"}],"tags":["all-months"],"title":"Review practice: Databricks SQL and DAX","track":"D","why_html":"<p>Security SQL and report measures carry outsized risk. A grant to one person survives their move to another team. A row filter written in the wrong dialect leaves a table open. A DAX measure with the wrong filter context shows a plausible number to every viewer of a dashboard. Reviewing these few lines carefully protects many readers.</p>"}
